15	// knew only what this view had launched. An image scanned from `:sec` — the same
16	// image, the same cache entry — went unnoticed here, so `S` offered itself on a
17	// row already being scanned and the two wrote the same file.
18	//
19	// The view's own `spinner.Model` stays, and deliberately: it animates *loading*
20	// — the image list, the networks, a `docker` action on a row — and a load is not
21	// a job. What moved is the frame the scan cells use, which now comes from the
22	// one chain the router holds (D5).
